  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a medium saucepan of salted water to the boil for the pasta. Cut the broccoli into large florets (see Make it yours). Finely chop the onion. Coarsely grate the cheese.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/465675/photos/large/74582_1-f957fec456f62a6ea7b1e490018e040b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook pasta and broccoli: Cook the pasta in the pan of boiling water for 5 mins. Add the broccoli and cook for a further 2 mins or until the pasta is al dente and the broccoli is tender. Drain. Transfer the broccoli to a bowl and cover to keep warm.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/465676/photos/large/74582_2-68f404d8514f7f67b74bb00750ff41b2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Start sauce: Meanwhile, heat 2 tsp olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the onion, stirring, for 3-4 mins until softened. Add the Italian seasoning and 1 tbs plain flour and cook, stirring, for 1 min or until golden. Add half the cream and stir until smooth. Stir in the tomatoes, 1 tsp sugar and 60ml (¼ cup) water and bring to the boil.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/465677/photos/large/74582_3-03eb4a269b90b16bc825fdf9943d5c5e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer sauce: Reduce the heat to medium and cook the sauce, stirring occasionally, for 5 mins or until thickened. Add the pasta and half the cheese and stir to combine. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/465678/photos/large/74582_4-449aa297ad312d285b3215448e7492cf.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the mac 'n' cheese and broccoli among bowls. Scatter over the remaining cheese and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/465679/photos/large/74582_5-938e3fc2267e6d158efc45c0e71185a2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: We also love our broccoli garlicky and pan-fried! Simply cut the broccoli into smaller florets and pan-fry in a little olive oil and garlic for 5 mins or until tender but still with crunch.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/465680/photos/large/74582_6-c945bb8f81a2a35fcf1975f678bc046f.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
